A||||35||batboy||I'm meeting a Fiero Lady||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||06-13-2000||12:04 AM||||Holy cow! Just got off the phone with a Fiero lady. I spoke to her son a couple months ago at a auto swap meet (where I had a sign posted about wanting to buy Fiero parts or whole cars). I finally called her and we chatted for a long time on the phone. I have no idea what she looks like, but she sounds like a real nice person and is the same age as me. She bought a 85 GT a couple years ago, drove it one day, then let her son drive it. He overheated it and now it don't run. It's been sitting in her yard ever since. She lives about a mile from my parents house. We have a lot in common, she's divorced, likes Fieros, we grew up in the same social-eco environment and area (although she went to a rival high school), etc. She's been hoping to get her Fiero fixed back up, but can't seem to ever scrape up enough money to do so, so she's considering selling it and asked me over to look at it the next time I visit my folks.<P>What should I do? We certainly chatted about lots more than Fieros and she seems very bright. I enjoyed talking to her, which I can't say about a lot of women. Would it be totally uncool if I went and looked at her Fiero and then asked her out? I'm completely clueless about the dating scene now, it's been so long. I'd probably be too shy or scared anyway...damn it...I'm babbling like an idiot. Well, at the very least, maybe I can pick up a cheap Fiero. Supposedly, the body is in excellent condition...I don't know about hers...LOL. Ok, I'll shut up now, I'm embarressing myself.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||06-13-2000||12:30 AM||||Hey Batboy, GO FOR IT!||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||06-13-2000||12:40 AM||||Well batboy it comes down to this.......<BR>Do you want her.....?  or the Fiero?<BR>you can't have both. ye see if you <BR>take her, then you would have to fix the fiero for her   ??? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> remember you said she wanted to fix it but did not have<BR>the $$$, well thats were you come in <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And that's not all bad!!!  IF she's not <BR>all bad.   You know what I mean!!<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000003||Fret Naught||06-13-2000||12:54 AM||||I say meet her, and offer to help her fix it up, can you think of a better bonding agent, common interest, than the Fiero? She probably doesn't have the $$$ because she is looking at what it would cost to pay someone to work on it, not do it as a hobby. I would give my left nut if my wife showed half the interest in my hobby that I do. And remember, no matter how good looking she is somebody somewhere is sick to death of her <BR>B!tch!%&  Looks aren't everything, and a vivacious good personality are worth thier wieght in gold. I think I am a little opinionated. ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Spyder||06-13-2000||01:02 AM||||batboy is giddy!!<BR>That’s great!<P>Hummmmm, <BR>What is the worst thing she could say to you….?<P>Ok, seriously, this is what I would do.<BR>You have to call her first to tell her when you will be visiting the family (an additional time to talk *wink* ) At this time you can ask her when a good time to come by and see the “car” (*wink, wink*) This way she can tell you when she will be there. Also at this time you can tell her that you will call her before you come over, and this is another time to make small talk.  And when you do see her, (the car?) you should know if you want her (the car?) If things go good, you could just load her up and take her back home (the car?)<BR>Keep Us Posted||||reg||3
Z||000005||FieroGTGirl||06-13-2000||02:29 AM||||Batboy~~<P>I don't see anything wrong with you asking her out. Apparently the two of you seemed to have hit it off real well in your conversations, that's always a good start.  <B>Just be yourself...Trust your instincts!</B>  Don't put undue pressure on yourself just because you've been out of the dating scene for awhile.  <B>GOOD LUCK!</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||06-13-2000||02:32 AM||||I say go work on her!  I mean, her FIERO...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Patrick||06-13-2000||02:57 AM||||<BR>Hey batboy, my advice (for what it's worth) is to just concentrate on the Fiero. Otherwise you're gonna put a lot of pressure on yourself before you even have any idea what this woman looks like. I agree with Fret that a good personality is extremely important, but there are certain physical attributes that we all, as individuals, prefer in a potential mate. When you go to check out the car, obviously you're going to get a chance to check out this woman. If you like what you see, <B><I>and if SHE appears to like what SHE sees</I></B>, then take it from there. Don't set yourself up for a fall by getting all stressed out for possibly nothing. The less you expect, the more pleasantly surprised you may become. Good luck, and make sure you share the details. (All of them! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>Of course, following advice on how to deal with women from a 44 year old single guy may not be the most rational thing for anyone to do...||||reg||14
Z||000008||sdm1964||06-13-2000||05:15 AM||||It sounds like you might be onto something, Like they said don't put any undo pressure on yourself. You will do fine, and good luck.||||reg||14
Z||000009||87ECO5||06-13-2000||07:22 AM||||I agree with Patrick.  I believe that's the best approach.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ThatRickGuy||06-13-2000||07:24 AM||||Hope for the best, plan for the worst. I met my current girl in a similar situation, talked to her a bit, then didn't see her for a long while, then we both had gotten out of pretty rough relationships, now we've been together for just short of 3 years. It was tastes in music that got us together, vice cars, but similar none the less. But anyway, I've messed up enough relationships to have built up a limited understanding of some of womens habbits (Their still confussing as heck, but you can figure out some little things). if she is a cutie when you see her, keep an eye open for her actions. is she wearing make up? is she acting a little nervious? who came out of the house first, her or her son (sending her son out first could show a bit of neviousnous). But anyways, there are a million and 1 little signs women give off.<P>But anyways, when it comes down to it, you'll either leave with a car, or a budding relationship w/ some common interests. Only problem is letter her drive it, my girl has been in 2 wrecks scince we started dating, I don't think she'll ever be driving the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||06-13-2000||07:41 AM||||Thanks for the input guys. I'm going over just to look at the Fiero, mainly. Sounds like she's ready to get rid of it cheap. But it does give me a good excuse to call her some more to "negotiate" the deal and to check her out to. Patrick: I wish you hadn't said that she'll be checking me out too. OMG, now I have to clean all the Fiero grease out from under my fingernails and maybe even put some deodorant on! I better drive the Batmobile too, just in case she wants to go for a ride. Oh no, that means I have to clean the car up to, oh guano! LOL You guys crack me up, you sound like my Mother. For all I know she lives with Bubba the biker dude or something or might even look like Attila the Hun. Sometimes you guys take me WAY too serious. This post was sort of tongue in cheek, although it would be great to meet a nice Fiero lady. I'll find out if she's online and give her a Forum card. Hope Cliff fixes the delete option in case I have to zap this topic so she don't see it!||||reg||1
