Z||000015||Sage||06-13-2000||09:26 AM||||When you get to the end, what will your regrets be...for things that you did, but maybe shouldn't have...or things that you didn't do that maybe you should have?<P>Meet her, size up the situation, trust your feelings.  Go Slow, you will be in enemy territory! LOL Check out the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Just my .002   Be <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||batboy||06-13-2000||09:59 AM||||Just for the record, I'm not into women who have more hair on their backs than I do.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> I know her son has a 1980 Camaro and is into high performance GM cars, so Raydar might be on to something. He seemed like a nice "kid" when I talked to him. Fret has a good idea too, I could suggest helping her work on it too, at least enough to find out what's really wrong with it, that way I could find out if she's afraid to get her hands dirty. Who knows, maybe the cooling system just needs burped.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 06-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||DRH||06-13-2000||01:42 PM||||Batboy,<P>Relax!!! I'm guessing she enjoyed the phone conversation as much as you did. Just pick it up where you left off on the phone... An offer to check out the car... A ride in the Batmobile to the local DQ for ice cream... Whatever feels right at the time, go with it. At the very least you'll probably make a new friend!<P>Going thru the son first is probably not a good idea... seems a little too "stalking".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||frontal lobe||06-13-2000||02:38 PM||||Sometimes you can get at least a clue of what the mother looks like by what the children look like, in this case the son.  Just imagine him without facial hair, sideburns, muscles, etc.  Then if you meet her and she doesn't have the "without", RUN, RUN, RUN FOR YOUR LIFE!  Seriously, if he isn't a bad looking guy (I know, this is hard to judge, we being guys) then there is at least a 50/50 chance it came from her.<P>Regarding her being from a rival high school, hey, this isn't "HOOSIERS".  (Sorry, you Indiana guys).||||reg||1
Z||000019||batboy||06-13-2000||03:05 PM||||DRH, I kind of like women who wear stockings. That was a typo in your post, right?<P>Doc, the son was a slender fellow and fairly handsome, for a guy. I'm not too worried about appearance at this point in my life, although totally hideous and obese women turn me off. Compatibility, honesty, intelligence, a sense of humor, and a good attitude towards life seem more important to me than beauty. Less sexual hang-ups then my exwife would be nice too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
